    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of June 03, 2022\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 09.06.2022)\n\nPROVINCIAL COUNCILS ELECTIONS(AMENDMENT)\n\nTo be presented in Parliament by Hon. Imthiaz Bakeer Markar, M.P.\n\nPrice : Rs. 12.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nThis Gazette Supplement can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nA\n\nto amend the Provincial Councils Elections Act, No. 2 of 1988\n\n(Private Members\u2019 Bill)\n\n1 Provincial Councils Elections (Amendment)\n\nShort title\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE PROVINCIAL COUNCILS ELECTIONSACT, NO. 2 OF 1988\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Provincial CouncilsElections (Amendment) Act, No. of 2022.\n\n2.The following new section is inserted immediatelyafter section 13 (8) (c) of the Provincial Councils ElectionsAct, No. 2 of 1988 and shall have effect as section 13 (9) inthe Principal Enactment:\u2014\n\n\u201c13 (9)(1) When submitting a nomination paper eachpolitical party or independent group shallensure that not less than one fourth of the totalnumber of candidates to be nominated for theElectoral District, and not less than one fourthof the total number of candidates in the districtlist, shall be youth candidates:\n\nProvided further that, the Commissioner ofElections shall, by notice published in theGazette, simultaneously with the call fornomination, specify the number of youthcandidates to be nominated on eachnomination list, in respect of eachadministrative district.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Clause, a youth shallbe defined as an individual either male orfemale of 35 years of age or less on the day ofthe calling of elections by the ElectionsCommissioner.\n\nAmendmentof section 13of theProvincialCouncilsElections Act\n\n2 Provincial Councils Elections (Amendment)"
