    "chunk_text": "\u201c(2) The office of President shall become vacant uponParliament passing, by not less than one half of thewhole number of Members of Parliament (includingthose not present), voting in its favour, a resolutionof no- confidence against the President, whichresolution may be introduced by a written noticeaddressed to the Speaker, signed by not less thanone third of the whole number of Members ofParliament.\u201d.\n\n11.Article 39 of the Constitution is hereby amended asfollows:\u2013\n\n(b) By the deletion of the words \u201cand shall appoint oneof the other Ministers of the Cabinet to act in theoffice of the Prime Minister\u201d in paragraph (2)thereof;\n\n(c) By the deletion of the proviso to paragraph (2),and the substitution therefor of the following newproviso:\u2013\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nAmendment ofArticle 38of theConstitution\n\nAmendment ofArticle 39of theConstitution\n\n9Twenty First Amendment to the Constitution\n\n\u201cProvided that if the Speaker is unable to act, theDeputy Speaker shall exercise, perform anddischarge the powers, duties and functions of theoffice of President during such period.\u201d.\n\n12.Article 40 of the Constitution is hereby repealed.\n\n13.Article 41 of the Constitution is hereby amended bythe addition of the following paragraph which shall haveeffect as the proviso to paragraph (1) of Article 41:\u2013\n\n\u201cProvided that the Cabinet of Ministers shalldetermine the maximum number of secretaries, officersand staff which may be so appointed.\u201d.\n\n14.Chapter VIIA of the Constitution is hereby repealedand the following Chapter substituted therefor:-\n\n\u201cCHAPTER VIIA\n\nTHE CONSTITUTIONAL COUNCIL\n\n41A. (1) There shall be a ConstitutionalCouncil (in this Chapter referred to as the\u201cCouncil\u201d) which shall consist of thefollowing members:\u2013\n\n(a) the Speaker;\n\n(b) the Prime Minister;\n\n(c) the Leader of the Opposition inParliament;\n\n(d) five persons appointed by thePresident, on the nomination of boththe Prime Minister and the Leader ofthe Opposition; and\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nRepealof Article40 of theConstitution."
