    "chunk_size_bytes": 1962,
    "chunk_text": "BE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Institution of BuildingServices Engineering & Technology of Sri Lanka(Incorporation) Act, No. of 2022.\n\nIncorporationof theInstitution ofBuildingServicesEngineering&Technologyof Sri Lanka.\n\nShort title\n\n25\n\nInstitution of Building Services Engineering &Technology of Sri Lanka (Incorporation)2\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n3.The general objects for which the Institution isconstituted are hereby declared to be\u2014\n\n(i)to foster and promote Building ServicesEngineering and Techonolgy as aprofession in Sri Lanka;\n\n(ii)to promote and safeguard the professionalstatus, interests, rights, powers, welfareand privileges of Building ServicesEngineers and Technologists to improvethe standards of Building ServicesEngineering and Technology in Sri Lanka;\n\n(iii)to enhance the standards of BuildingServices Engineering and Technology inSri Lanka;\n\n(iv)to offer the Government and its Agenciesa forum to discuss and ascertain the viewsof Building Services Engineering andTechnologists on matters directly orindirectly affecting the Profession;\n\n(v)to discuss with and obtain views ofInstitutions, Associations, Manufacturers,Contractors and other persons engaged inBuilding Services Engineering andTechnology on matters of common interest;\n\n(vi)to introduce general standards ofProfessional Conduct and Practice forBuliding Services Engineers andTechnologists and to ensure themaintenance of such standards in theirprofessional activities;\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation\n\n30\n\n3Institution of Building Services Engineering &Technology of Sri Lanka (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(vii)to determine scales of Professional Feesand conditions of engagement forBuilding Services Engineers andTechnologists, within Sri Lanka;\n\n(viii)to liaise with Institutions/Associations ofBuilding Services Engineers andTechnologists in other countries;"
