    "chunk_text": "Clause 24 : This clause amends section 59 of the principal enactment and is consequentialto the amendment made by clause 2.\n\nClause 25 : This clause amends section 60A of the principal enactment and isconsequential to the amendment made by clause 2.\n\nClause 27 : This clause replaces Schedule IV of the principal enactment and the newSchedule increases the amounts of monthly wages of an injured workman which is the basisfor payment of compensation, and amount of compensation payable in case of a death,permanent total disablement and, half monthly compensation for temporary disablementof workman.\n\nWorkmen\u2019s Compensation (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 62/2018\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE WORKMEN\u2019S COMPENSATION ORDINANCE(CHAPTER 139)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows: -\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Workmen\u2019sCompensation (Amendment) Act, No. \u2026\u2026 of 2022.\n\n2. The long title to the Workmen\u2019s CompensationOrdinance (Chapter 139) (hereinafter in this Act referred toas the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is hereby amended by thesubstitution, for the words \u201cwho are injured in the course oftheir employment.\u201d of the words \u201cwho are injured in thecourse of their employment or while coming from their placeof residence to the work place or while returing back to theirplace of residence from the work place.\u201d.\n\n3. Section 2 of the principal enactment is hereby amendedby the insertion immediately after the definition of theexpression \u201cpartial disablement\u201d of the followingdefinition:\u2013\n\n\u201c\u201cplace of residence\u201d includes any permanent place ofresidence of a workman or a boarding house or anyother place where a workman resides temporarily forthe purpose of coming to his workplace;\u201d."
